      {
        "id": 169195,
        "name": "BlueHairedMeerkat",
        "username": "BlueHairedMeerkat",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/bluehairedmeerkat/{size}/1967_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-03-23T11:10:39.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"robb8888\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/r/dec6dc/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> robb8888:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Sigh</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Yes, pretty much any villain can have a lucky draw and unexpectedly wreck face, and that's great. Hell, I got beaten by <em>Gloomweaver</em> the other day! And it was a great game, because it let me see the damage Gloomy (usually a pushover) could do with a good draw. &nbsp;I for one really like this type of One-Shot, as a 'hey, here's what this villain can&nbsp; <em>really</em>  do'. Keep up the good work, Handelabra.</p>",
