      {
        "id": 169201,
        "name": "hstein3",
        "username": "hstein3",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/hstein3/{size}/2159_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-03-25T13:48:55.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"BlueHairedMeerkat\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/bluehairedmeerkat/48/1967_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> BlueHairedMeerkat:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Yes, pretty much any villain can have a lucky draw and unexpectedly wreck face, and that's great. Hell, I got beaten by <em>Gloomweaver</em> the other day! And it was a great game, because it let me see the damage Gloomy (usually a pushover) could do with a good draw.&nbsp;I for one really like this type of One-Shot, as a 'hey, here's what this villain can&nbsp;<em>really</em> do'. Keep up the good work, Handelabra.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Oh, Gloomweaver can get brutal, especially if he gets all three relics into play. (Such as the one-shot that featured him a few weeks ago.)&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 31,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:51:27.544Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
